  "dataset_bias_disclosure": "This dataset is sourced ENTIRELY from Swift's own self-reported Discord recaps (two session days, operator-supplied screenshots, hand-transcribed, never fabricated). By construction it is almost entirely a WINNER population: 2026-10-21 is 22-0 (channel's own stated record, zero losers) and 2026-10-19 has exactly ONE row marked 'loss' despite a nominal +4.35% gain, whose classification basis is unknown (flagged, not resolved). The operator's own instruction was to 'study all examples, including losses -- not just the biggest winners.' Swift's channel cannot supply that losing population by its own stated nature (it is a highlight/recap feed), so Night Hawk's OWN real historical losing 0DTE commits must supply the loss side of this study -- that is a separate, not-yet-built follow-up (see docs/audit/0DTE-RESEARCH.md E7), not something this consolidation invents or approximates from the Swift data itself.",
  "missing_fields_disclosure": "Neither source screenshot carries exact alert/entry/exit timestamps -- only date, contract, entry/exit premium, and %. Every trade in this dataset is missing alert_ts/entry_ts/exit_ts for that reason (see each trade's own `missing_fields`); this is a property of the source material, not an extraction gap. `zerodte-swift-comparison.mjs` substitutes a real-minute-bar price-match-window as an observable-timing PROXY where an exact timestamp is required -- that proxy is a separate, disclosed approximation, not a claim that the true timestamp is known."
